{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions"},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Put every event a tracker tracks in a session, and sample whole sessions."}],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Putting-events-in-sessions","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/Events\/Enricher\/sessions(kinds:file:fileID:function:line:column:)","doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/Events\/Enricher\/sessions(timeout:kinds:file:fileID:function:line:column:)","doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/SessionEventKind","doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/NonPositiveSessionTimeout"],"title":"Putting events in sessions"},{"anchor":"Session-events","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/SessionStarted","doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/SessionEnded"],"title":"Session events"},{"anchor":"Sampling-whole-sessions","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/Trackers\/Sampler\/sessions(where:rate:)"],"title":"Sampling whole sessions"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Sessions are opt-in. Add the sessions enricher to the ones a tracker is built with, and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tracker’s worker sets each record’s "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/SessionKey","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" to its session’s identifier. A session"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"goes on while each event comes less than the timeout (30 minutes by default) after the one before it,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"measured between the records’ timestamps. The first event after a longer gap starts a new session."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The enricher tracks ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/SessionStarted","isActive":true},{"text":" before each session’s first event, and ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/SessionEnded","isActive":true},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"before that from the second session on, carrying the ended session’s duration. A run’s last session","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"has no ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/SessionEnded","isActive":true},{"text":": a session ends only when an event comes after the timeout. Pass ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"kinds:"},{"text":" to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"track only one kind of session event, or neither; every record still carries its key.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A session’s identifier is a version 7 UUID: the session’s start in Unix milliseconds, then random","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"bits. The enricher holds it in memory only, and a new tracker, as on the next launch, starts a new","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"session. A store keeps it beside each record of the session, and it is deleted when the store","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"deletes the record’s bytes (a ","type":"text"},{"code":"SegmentStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": once its whole segment is delivered), so a record","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"recovered after a relaunch still carries the session it was tracked in. The key,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/SessionKey"},{"text":", is in the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Events","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" module.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sampler.sessions(rate:)"},{"type":"text","text":" keeps or drops every record of a session alike, its session events with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it, by the record’s "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/SessionKey","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". It needs the sessions enricher among the tracker’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"enrichers."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For the app, device, operating system, locale and network an event was tracked on, use","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"StandardContext","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". For the app’s opens and moves to the background, use ","type":"text"},{"code":"LifecycleTracking","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its ","type":"text"},{"code":"ApplicationOpened","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" after a long time in the background starts a new session here, though","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"neither module knows about the other.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import Sessions","import Trackers","","let tracker = Tracker(enrichers: [try .sessions(timeout: .seconds(15 * 60), kinds: [.started])])","tracker.track(SignedUp(plan: \"pro\"))  \/\/ tracks SessionStarted, then SignedUp, both with the same SessionKey"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The guide "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/sessionsandstandardcontext","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"covers sessions beside the standard context, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/samplingevents","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"covers sampling."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"patc